            <div xml:id="d985">

                <pb facs="1316" n="1192" xml:id="pg1192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.111/140: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-08-06T18:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 6,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received August 6—1:59
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>203. My telegram number 202, August 2[<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>], 10 a.m. As
                    result of my representations Adnan Bey informed me this morning that naturalized
                    Americans of Hellenic (non-Ottoman) origin, as well as naturalized Americans of
                    Russian-Armenian origin, will be permitted to enter Turkey freely. He assured me
                    that should naturalized Americans of Ottoman origin arrive Turkey they will not
                    be arrested but will be requested by the police to leave the country, and he
                    further assured me that I would be notified in each case.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
